SUMMARY:October Writers Workshop at Watchung Booksellers
DESCRIPTION:Watchung Booksellers hosts a writers’ workshop for creatives who are stuck in their process with therapist Amos Kamil on Sunday\, October 25 afrom 6:00 – 8:00 p.m. \nStuck isn’t a discipline problem. Most workshops on creative block treat it as a craft problem — outline more\, write badly on purpose\, lower the stakes. Useful\, but it treats the symptom. As a therapist who works with writers and creative people\, Amos Kamil goes one layer deeper: block is usually not a craft failure\, it’s a psychological pattern doing its job (protecting against exposure\, failure\, an old judgment) and it responds to different tools than craft advice does. \nThe workshop’s promise: leave having identified your specific sabotage pattern and practiced one concrete tool against it\, live. In this introductory workshop\, you’ll leave with: \n*A named pattern (your own version of the “quiet agent” derailing you)\n*One practiced tool you can use again unassisted\n*A one-line diagnosis of where your current project is stuck in the larger arc\, not just “stuck” \nTickets are $80 for the two-hour introductory workshop. Purchase at watchungbooksellers.com. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/october-writers-workshop-at-watchung-booksellers/
LOCATION:watchung booksellers the kids’ room\, 44 Fairfield St.\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:General Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/wwoct.png
END:VEVENT
